How Breadsticks Are Made

Commercial breadsticks are produced through a series of carefully controlled manufacturing steps.

The process typically includes:

Mixing the dough – Ingredients are blended until the dough reaches the desired consistency.
Fermentation – The dough rests to develop flavor and structure.
Shaping – Automated equipment forms the dough into evenly sized breadsticks.
Baking – Breadsticks are baked at controlled temperatures to achieve their signature crispness and golden color.
Cooling – Products cool before packaging to preserve texture.
Packaging – Breadsticks are sealed to help maintain freshness during storage and transportation.

Each stage is carefully monitored to ensure product consistency.

